      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person must be a resident of Australia.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The conduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly outside Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 5  Attorney-General’s consent required",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a01078#sch-1-sec-73-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2004a01078.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a01078.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against this Subdivision must not be\ncommenced without the Attorney-General’s written consent.\n\n(2) However, a person may be arrested, charged, remanded in custody\nor released on bail in connection with an offence against this\nSubdivision before the necessary consent has been given.\nSubdivision B—Document offences related to people smuggling\nand unlawful entry into foreign countries",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against this Subdivision must not be\ncommenced without the Attorney-General’s written consent.\n\n(2) However, a person may be arrested, charged, remanded in custody\nor released on bail in connection with an offence against this\nSubdivision before the necessary consent has been given.\nSubdivision B—Document offences related to people smuggling\nand unlawful entry into foreign countries",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-5-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "847995a6001b78374dcad52da89492501920904d2a9460cf7b1cfffa1e4cf9d4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a01078#sch-1-sec-73-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "73 5  Attorney-General’s consent required",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against this Subdivision must not be\ncommenced without the Attorney-General’s written consent.\n\n(2) However, a person may be arrested, charged, remanded in custody\nor released on bail in connection with an offence against this\nSubdivision before the necessary consent has been given.\nSubdivision B—Document offences related to people smuggling\nand unlawful entry into foreign countries"
    },
