    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 9  Providing or possessing a travel or identity document issued or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a01078#sch-1-sec-73-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2004a01078.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a01078.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "altered dishonestly or as a result of threats\n\n(1) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person provides or possesses a travel or identity\ndocument; and\n\n(b) the first person knows that:\n\n(i) the issue of the travel or identity document; or\n\n(ii) an alteration of the travel or identity document;\n\nhas been obtained dishonestly or by threats; and\n\n(c) the first person intends that the document will be used to\nfacilitate the entry of another person (the other person) into a\nforeign country, where the entry of the other person into the\nforeign country would not comply with the requirements\nunder that country’s law for entry into the country; and\n\n(d) the first person provided or possessed the document:\n\n(i) having obtained (whether directly or indirectly) a\nbenefit to do so; or\n\n(ii) with the intention of obtaining (whether directly or\nindirectly) a benefit.\n\nSchedule 1  People smuggling",
      "skos:definition": "altered dishonestly or as a result of threats\n\n(1) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person provides or possesses a travel or identity\ndocument; and\n\n(b) the first person knows that:\n\n(i) the issue of the travel or identity document; or\n\n(ii) an alteration of the travel or identity document;\n\nhas been obtained dishonestly or by threats; and\n\n(c) the first person intends that the document will be used to\nfacilitate the entry of another person (the other person) into a\nforeign country, where the entry of the other person into the\nforeign country would not comply with the requirements\nunder that country’s law for entry into the country; and\n\n(d) the first person provided or possessed the document:\n\n(i) having obtained (whether directly or indirectly) a\nbenefit to do so; or\n\n(ii) with the intention of obtaining (whether directly or\nindirectly) a benefit.\n\nSchedule 1  People smuggling",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-9-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "165d6399c009f14a9c1421eea470507327bcc50456879f5d69fb0d5003d9f78e",
      "skos:note": "Providing or possessing a travel or identity document issued or altered dishonestly or as a result of threats is an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a01078#sch-1-sec-73-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "73 9  Providing or possessing a travel or identity document issued or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "altered dishonestly or as a result of threats\n\n(1) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person provides or possesses a travel or identity\ndocument; and\n\n(b) the first person knows that:\n\n(i) the issue of the travel or identity document; or\n\n(ii) an alteration of the travel or identity document;\n\nhas been obtained dishonestly or by threats; and\n\n(c) the first person intends that the document will be used to\nfacilitate the entry of another person (the other person) into a\nforeign country, where the entry of the other person into the\nforeign country would not comply with the requirements\nunder that country’s law for entry into the country; and\n\n(d) the first person provided or possessed the document:\n\n(i) having obtained (whether directly or indirectly) a\nbenefit to do so; or\n\n(ii) with the intention of obtaining (whether directly or\nindirectly) a benefit.\n\nSchedule 1  People smuggling"
    },
    {
