    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 11  Taking possession of or destroying another person’s travel or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a01078#sch-1-sec-73-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2004a01078.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a01078.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "identity document\n\nA person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\nPeople smuggling  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (People Smuggling, Firearms Trafficking and Other Measures)\n\n(a) the first person takes possession of, or destroys, a travel or\nidentity document that applies to another person (the other\nperson); and\n\n(b) the first person does so intending to conceal the other\nperson’s identity or nationality; and\n\n(c) at the time of doing so, the first person intends to organise or\nfacilitate the entry of the other person into a foreign country:\n\n(i) having obtained, or with the intention of obtaining,\nwhether directly or indirectly, a benefit to organise or\nfacilitate that entry; and\n\n(ii) where the entry of the other person into the foreign\ncountry would not comply with the requirements under\nthat country’s law for entry into the country.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.",
      "skos:definition": "identity document\n\nA person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\nPeople smuggling  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (People Smuggling, Firearms Trafficking and Other Measures)\n\n(a) the first person takes possession of, or destroys, a travel or\nidentity document that applies to another person (the other\nperson); and\n\n(b) the first person does so intending to conceal the other\nperson’s identity or nationality; and\n\n(c) at the time of doing so, the first person intends to organise or\nfacilitate the entry of the other person into a foreign country:\n\n(i) having obtained, or with the intention of obtaining,\nwhether directly or indirectly, a benefit to organise or\nfacilitate that entry; and\n\n(ii) where the entry of the other person into the foreign\ncountry would not comply with the requirements under\nthat country’s law for entry into the country.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-1-sec-73-11-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d9059c8cd4a90d69e38e655c7aaa5257af09200539ef85231efdcd4392ffc038",
      "skos:note": "Taking possession of or destroying another person's travel or identity document without intention to conceal their identity or nationality is not prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a01078#sch-1-sec-73-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "73 11  Taking possession of or destroying another person’s travel or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "identity document\n\nA person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:\n\nPeople smuggling  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (People Smuggling, Firearms Trafficking and Other Measures)\n\n(a) the first person takes possession of, or destroys, a travel or\nidentity document that applies to another person (the other\nperson); and\n\n(b) the first person does so intending to conceal the other\nperson’s identity or nationality; and\n\n(c) at the time of doing so, the first person intends to organise or\nfacilitate the entry of the other person into a foreign country:\n\n(i) having obtained, or with the intention of obtaining,\nwhether directly or indirectly, a benefit to organise or\nfacilitate that entry; and\n\n(ii) where the entry of the other person into the foreign\ncountry would not comply with the requirements under\nthat country’s law for entry into the country.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth."
    },
