    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-2-sec-360-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360 3  Taking or sending a firearm across borders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2004a01078#sch-2-sec-360-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2004a01078.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a01078.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) in the course of trade or commerce among the States,\nbetween Territories or between a Territory and a State, the\nperson takes or sends a firearm from one State or Territory to\nanother State or Territory; and\n\n(b) the person does so intending that the firearm will be disposed\nof in the other State or Territory (whether by the person or\nanother); and\n\n(c) the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether:\n\n(i) the disposal of the firearm; or\n\n(ii) any acquisition of the firearm that results from the\ndisposal;\n\nwould happen in circumstances that would constitute an\noffence against the firearm law of that other State or\nTerritory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or a fine of 2,500 penalty\nunits, or both.\n\n(2) In this section:\n\nSchedule 2  Cross-border firearms trafficking",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:\n\n(a) in the course of trade or commerce among the States,\nbetween Territories or between a Territory and a State, the\nperson takes or sends a firearm from one State or Territory to\nanother State or Territory; and\n\n(b) the person does so intending that the firearm will be disposed\nof in the other State or Territory (whether by the person or\nanother); and\n\n(c) the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether:\n\n(i) the disposal of the firearm; or\n\n(ii) any acquisition of the firearm that results from the\ndisposal;\n\nwould happen in circumstances that would constitute an\noffence against the firearm law of that other State or\nTerritory.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or a fine of 2,500 penalty\nunits, or both.\n\n(2) In this section:\n\nSchedule 2  Cross-border firearms trafficking",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-2-sec-360-3-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-2-sec-360-3-ss-2"
        }
      ],
