      },
      "dc:source": "c2004a01078.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(1C) If a court of summary jurisdiction convicts a person of an offence\nagainst subsection (1) in accordance with subsection (1B), the\npenalty that the court may impose is a sentence of imprisonment\nnot exceeding 2 years or a fine not exceeding 120 penalty units, or\nboth.",
      "skos:definition": "(1C) If a court of summary jurisdiction convicts a person of an offence\nagainst subsection (1) in accordance with subsection (1B), the\npenalty that the court may impose is a sentence of imprisonment\nnot exceeding 2 years or a fine not exceeding 120 penalty units, or\nboth.",
      "values:partOf": {
