      "dc:source": "c2004a01078.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "Criminal Code)\nRepeal the paragraphs, substitute:\n\n(a) the official falsely represents himself or herself to be a\nCommonwealth public official in a particular capacity; and\n\n(b) the official does so in the course of doing an act, or attending\na place, in the assumed capacity of such an official.",
      "skos:definition": "Criminal Code)\nRepeal the paragraphs, substitute:\n\n(a) the official falsely represents himself or herself to be a\nCommonwealth public official in a particular capacity; and\n\n(b) the official does so in the course of doing an act, or attending\na place, in the assumed capacity of such an official.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-3-sec-17-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2004a01078-sch-3-sec-17-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "841032e49273d8e078163e795f7db544dbd31ed3197b495f4c3b9fbfc2191ac2",
      "skos:note": "Official cannot falsely represent themselves as a Commonwealth public official."
    },
    {
